What the licence above covers in THIS repository
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository contains no source code. For the purposes of the licence
above, "the Software" is what this repository actually holds: the
documentation (README.md, DOCKERHUB.md), the Compose file
(docker-compose.yml) and the environment template (.env.example). Copy
them, change them, use them in your own setup, ship them with your own
work -- MIT, nothing further asked.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
What it does NOT cover: the container image
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The TecGate image (docker.io/amslertec/tecgate) is distributed from Docker
Hub, not from this repository, and the grant above says nothing about it.
Its terms travel inside it: the image carries its licence texts at
/usr/share/licenses/tecgate/LICENSE and
/usr/share/licenses/owasp-crs/LICENSE, and those are the ones that apply
to the software it runs -- among them the Apache License 2.0 of the
bundled OWASP Core Rule Set, whose obligations MIT does not lift.

Two things follow, and neither is a formality:

  - Reading or copying this repository grants no right in the image.
  - The image is supplied with no warranty of any kind either. This is
    one installation's tooling, published in case it is useful, not a
    product with support behind it.

